description:
Design a binary counter that counts from 0 to 9 in a specified number of bits (N=4 by default). On each positive clock edge, the counter increments its value; when it reaches 9, it resets back to 0. The current count value is output through the 'out' port. This module is useful for applications requiring a simple count-up function with reset capabilities.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [N-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [N-1:0] out
);parameter N = 4; // number of bits in the counter

reg [N-1:0] count;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (count == 9) begin
    count <= 0;
  end else begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end
end

assign out = count;

endmodule

