description:
Design a simple state machine that controls a user authentication signal based on input conditions. The circuit has an enable signal (`on`) and a numeric input (`num`). When `on` is low, the output `on_out` goes low, effectively locking the access. If `on` is high and `num` is true, the output `on_out` is set to high, allowing access. This module essentially acts as a password toggle mechanism, maintaining the access state unless specifically reset by the `on` signal.
module top_module(
	input on,
	input num,
	output on_out
    );

code:
module top_module(
	input on,
	input num,
	output on_out
    );reg temp=1;
assign on_out=temp;

always @(*)
begin
	if(temp==1 && on==0) temp<=0;
	else if(temp==0 && on==1) 
	begin
		if(num) temp<=1;
	end
end

endmodule

