Design a 4-bit to 7-segment display decoder. The module takes a 4-bit binary input (num) representing a decimal digit (0-9) and outputs the corresponding 7-segment display encoding (display) that lights up the appropriate segments to visually represent the digit. The output uses a combination of bits to indicate which segments are active, providing a direct way to display numeric values on a 7-segment display.
