description:
Design a synchronous communication channel module that captures a two-bit input from signals l0 and l1 on the falling edge of the enable signal le, storing it in a buffer. This module utilizes a delay buffer to output the captured data on r0 and r1, which represent the delayed version of the inputs. The captured data is only updated when le transitions from high to low, ensuring that data integrity is maintained during the communication process.
module top_module(
    input wire l0, l1,
    output wire le,
    input wire r0, r1
);

code:
module top_module(
    input wire l0, l1,
    output wire le,
    input wire r0, r1
);reg [1:0] buffer;
reg [1:0] delay_buffer;

always @(posedge le) begin
    delay_buffer <= buffer;
end

always @(posedge le or negedge le) begin
    if (!le) begin
        buffer <= {l1, l0};
    end
end

assign r0 = delay_buffer[0];
assign r1 = delay_buffer[1];

endmodule

