description:
Design a reset bridge that generates a synchronous reset signal output, srst_n, based on a clock signal, clk, and an active-low asynchronous reset signal, arst_n. When arst_n is asserted low, the internal state register q is initialized to zero. On each positive clock edge, the design shifts the values within q, setting the least significant bit to high, while simultaneously passing the third element of a buffer to the output srst_n. This effectively creates a delayed version of the reset signal that can be used for system synchronization purposes.
module top_module(
    input clk,    
    input arst_n,  

    output reg srst_n


);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,    
    input arst_n,  

    output reg srst_n


);reg [2:0] q;
reg [2:0] buffer;

always @(posedge clk or negedge arst_n) begin
    if(~arst_n) begin
        q <= 'h0;
    end 
    else begin
         q[2] <= q[1];
         q[1] <= q[0];
         q[0] <= 1'b1;
    end
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    srst_n <= buffer[2];
    buffer[2] <= buffer[1];
    buffer[1] <= buffer[0];
    buffer[0] <= q[2];
end 


endmodule

